# .dockerignore -- ALLOWLIST, not a denylist.
#
# This file used to list what to exclude, and it fell behind the repo: it predated .venv-airflow
# (170 MB), the DVC cache (44 GB) and weights/ (6 GB), so `docker build` was streaming a 50.5 GB
# context to build a ~1 GB image. A denylist here is a standing bug -- it is wrong again the next
# time anyone adds a big directory, and nothing fails loudly when it does.
#
# So: exclude everything, then re-include exactly the four paths serve.Dockerfile COPYs. A new
# directory is ignored by default; a new COPY that needs something has to add it here, and the
# build fails loudly if it forgets.

*

!app
!src
!pyproject.toml
!requirements-serve.txt

# serve-cloud.Dockerfile only. Gitignored (24 MB of weights) and absent until
# scripts/export_champion.py has run -- serve.Dockerfile COPYs nothing from it, so a missing
# export costs the base build nothing and fails the cloud build loudly, which is correct.
!build/champion

# Re-excluded AFTER the allowlist (last match wins) -- these live inside app/ and src/ and are
# rebuilt in the image anyway.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
